\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"# Testing Anti-Patterns\\\\n\\\\n**Load this reference when:** writing or changing tests, adding mocks, or tempted to add test-only methods to production code.\\\\n\\\\n## Overview\\\\n\\\\nTest\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0ms must verify real behavior, not mock behavior. Mocks are a means to isolate, not the thing being tested.\\\\n\\\\n**Core principle:** Test what the code does, not what the mocks do.\\\\n\\\\n**Following strict TDD prevents t\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mhese anti-patterns.**\\\\n\\\\n## The Iron Laws\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n1. NEVER test mock behavior\\\\n2. NEVER add test-only methods to production classes\\\\n3. NEVER mock without understanding dependencies\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Anti-Pattern 1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m: Testing Mock Behavior\\\\n\\\\n**The violation:**\\\\n```typescript\\\\n// ❌ BAD: Testing that the mock exists\\\\ntest('renders sidebar', () => {\\\\n  render(<Page />);\\\\n  expect(screen.getByTestId('sidebar-mock')).toBeInThe\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mDocument();\\\\n});\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Why this is wrong:**\\\\n- You're verifying the mock works, not that the component works\\\\n- Test passes when mock is present, fails when it's not\\\\n- Tells you nothing about real behavior\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m\\\\n\\\\n**your human partner's correction:** \\\\\\\"Are we testing the behavior of a mock?\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**The fix:**\\\\n```typescript\\\\n// ✅ GOOD: Test real component or don't mock it\\\\ntest('renders sidebar', () => {\\\\n  rende\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mr(<Page />);  // Don't mock sidebar\\\\n  expect(screen.getByRole('navigation')).toBeInTheDocument();\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\n// OR if sidebar must be mocked for isolation:\\\\n// Don't assert on the mock - test Page's behavior with s\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0midebar present\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Gate Function\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nBEFORE asserting on any mock element:\\\\n  Ask: \\\\\\\"Am I testing real component behavior or just mock existence?\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  IF testing mock existence:\\\\n    STOP -\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m Delete the assertion or unmock the component\\\\n\\\\n  Test real behavior instead\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Anti-Pattern 2: Test-Only Methods in Production\\\\n\\\\n**The violation:**\\\\n```typescript\\\\n// ❌ BAD: destroy() only used in \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mtests\\\\nclass Session {\\\\n  async destroy() {  // Looks like production API!\\\\n    await this._workspaceManager?.destroyWorkspace(this.id);\\\\n    // ... cleanup\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n// In tests\\\\nafterEach(() => session.des\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mtroy());\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Why this is wrong:**\\\\n- Production class polluted with test-only code\\\\n- Dangerous if accidentally called in production\\\\n- Violates YAGNI and separation of concerns\\\\n- Confuses object lifecyc\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mle with entity lifecycle\\\\n\\\\n**The fix:**\\\\n```typescript\\\\n// ✅ GOOD: Test utilities handle test cleanup\\\\n// Session has no destroy() - it's stateless in production\\\\n\\\\n// In test-utils/\\\\nexport async function cl\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0meanupSession(session: Session) {\\\\n  const workspace = session.getWorkspaceInfo();\\\\n  if (workspace) {\\\\n    await workspaceManager.destroyWorkspace(workspace.id);\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n// In tests\\\\nafterEach(() => cleanup\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mSession(session));\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Gate Function\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nBEFORE adding any method to production class:\\\\n  Ask: \\\\\\\"Is this only used by tests?\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  IF yes:\\\\n    STOP - Don't add it\\\\n    Put it in test utili\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mties instead\\\\n\\\\n  Ask: \\\\\\\"Does this class own this resource's lifecycle?\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  IF no:\\\\n    STOP - Wrong class for this method\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Anti-Pattern 3: Mocking Without Understanding\\\\n\\\\n**The violation:*\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m*\\\\n```typescript\\\\n// ❌ BAD: Mock breaks test logic\\\\ntest('detects duplicate server', () => {\\\\n  // Mock prevents config write that test depends on!\\\\n  vi.mock('ToolCatalog', () => ({\\\\n    discoverAndCacheTools: \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mvi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined)\\\\n  }));\\\\n\\\\n  await addServer(config);\\\\n  await addServer(config);  // Should throw - but won't!\\\\n});\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Why this is wrong:**\\\\n- Mocked method had side effect test d\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mepended on (writing config)\\\\n- Over-mocking to \\\\\\\"be safe\\\\\\\" breaks actual behavior\\\\n- Test passes for wrong reason or fails mysteriously\\\\n\\\\n**The fix:**\\\\n```typescript\\\\n// ✅ GOOD: Mock at correct level\\\\ntest\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m('detects duplicate server', () => {\\\\n  // Mock the slow part, preserve behavior test needs\\\\n  vi.mock('MCPServerManager'); // Just mock slow server startup\\\\n\\\\n  await addServer(config);  // Config written\\\\n  awa\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mit addServer(config);  // Duplicate detected ✓\\\\n});\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Gate Function\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nBEFORE mocking any method:\\\\n  STOP - Don't mock yet\\\\n\\\\n  1. Ask: \\\\\\\"What side effects does the real method have?\\\\\\\"\\\\n \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m 2. Ask: \\\\\\\"Does this test depend on any of those side effects?\\\\\\\"\\\\n  3. Ask: \\\\\\\"Do I fully understand what this test needs?\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  IF depends on side effects:\\\\n    Mock at lower level (the actual slow/extern\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mal operation)\\\\n    OR use test doubles that preserve necessary behavior\\\\n    NOT the high-level method the test depends on\\\\n\\\\n  IF unsure what test depends on:\\\\n    Run test with real implementation FIRST\\\\n    O\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mbserve what actually needs to happen\\\\n    THEN add minimal mocking at the right level\\\\n\\\\n  Red flags:\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"I'll mock this to be safe\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"This might be slow, better mock it\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - Mocking wit\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mhout understanding the dependency chain\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Anti-Pattern 4: Incomplete Mocks\\\\n\\\\n**The violation:**\\\\n```typescript\\\\n// ❌ BAD: Partial mock - only fields you think you need\\\\nconst mockResponse = {\\\\n  sta\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mtus: 'success',\\\\n  data: { userId: '123', name: 'Alice' }\\\\n  // Missing: metadata that downstream code uses\\\\n};\\\\n\\\\n// Later: breaks when code accesses response.metadata.requestId\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Why this is wrong:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m\\\\n- **Partial mocks hide structural assumptions** - You only mocked fields you know about\\\\n- **Downstream code may depend on fields you didn't include** - Silent failures\\\\n- **Tests pass but integration fails** - M\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mock incomplete, real API complete\\\\n- **False confidence** - Test proves nothing about real behavior\\\\n\\\\n**The Iron Rule:** Mock the COMPLETE data structure as it exists in reality, not just fields your immediate tes\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mt uses.\\\\n\\\\n**The fix:**\\\\n```typescript\\\\n// ✅ GOOD: Mirror real API completeness\\\\nconst mockResponse = {\\\\n  status: 'success',\\\\n  data: { userId: '123', name: 'Alice' },\\\\n  metadata: { requestId: 'req-789', tim\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mestamp: 1234567890 }\\\\n  // All fields real API returns\\\\n};\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Gate Function\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nBEFORE creating mock responses:\\\\n  Check: \\\\\\\"What fields does the real API response contain?\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  Actions:\\\\\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mn    1. Examine actual API response from docs/examples\\\\n    2. Include ALL fields system might consume downstream\\\\n    3. Verify mock matches real response schema completely\\\\n\\\\n  Critical:\\\\n    If you're creating\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m a mock, you must understand the ENTIRE structure\\\\n    Partial mocks fail silently when code depends on omitted fields\\\\n\\\\n  If uncertain: Include all documented fields\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Anti-Pattern 5: Integration Test\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0ms as Afterthought\\\\n\\\\n**The violation:**\\\\n```\\\\n✅ Implementation complete\\\\n❌ No tests written\\\\n\\\\\\\"Ready for testing\\\\\\\"\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Why this is wrong:**\\\\n- Testing is part of implementation, not optional follow\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m-up\\\\n- TDD would have caught this\\\\n- Can't claim complete without tests\\\\n\\\\n**The fix:**\\\\n```\\\\nTDD cycle:\\\\n1. Write failing test\\\\n2. Implement to pass\\\\n3. Refactor\\\\n4. THEN claim complete\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## When M\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mocks Become Too Complex\\\\n\\\\n**Warning signs:**\\\\n- Mock setup longer than test logic\\\\n- Mocking everything to make test pass\\\\n- Mocks missing methods real components have\\\\n- Test breaks when mock changes\\\\n\\\\n**yo\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mur human partner's question:** \\\\\\\"Do we need to be using a mock here?\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Consider:** Integration tests with real components often simpler than complex mocks\\\\n\\\\n## TDD Prevents These Anti-Patterns\\\\n\\\\n**Why\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m TDD helps:**\\\\n1. **Write test first** → Forces you to think about what you're actually testing\\\\n2. **Watch it fail** → Confirms test tests real behavior, not mocks\\\\n3. **Minimal implementation** → No test-only met\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mhods creep in\\\\n4. **Real dependencies** → You see what the test actually needs before mocking\\\\n\\\\n**If you're testing mock behavior, you violated TDD** - you added mocks without watching test fail against real code \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mfirst.\\\\n\\\\n## Quick Reference\\\\n\\\\n| Anti-Pattern | Fix |\\\\n|--------------|-----|\\\\n| Assert on mock elements | Test real component or unmock it |\\\\n| Test-only methods in production | Move to test utilities |\\\\n| M\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mock without understanding | Understand dependencies first, mock minimally |\\\\n| Incomplete mocks | Mirror real API completely |\\\\n| Tests as afterthought | TDD - tests first |\\\\n| Over-complex mocks | Consider integra\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mtion tests |\\\\n\\\\n## Red Flags\\\\n\\\\n- Assertion checks for `*-mock` test IDs\\\\n- Methods only called in test files\\\\n- Mock setup is >50% of test\\\\n- Test fails when you remove mock\\\\n- Can't explain why mock is neede\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0md\\\\n- Mocking \\\\\\\"just to be safe\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## The Bottom Line\\\\n\\\\n**Mocks are tools to isolate, not things to test.**\\\\n\\\\nIf TDD reveals you're testing mock behavior, you've gone wrong.\\\\n\\\\nFix: Test real behavior \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0mor question why you're mocking at all.\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n109\\\\r\\\\n112\\\\r\\\\n9c6c41e4 src/features/desktop-node/RipgrepClient.ts                             (Daichi Kimura 2026-07-14 00:32:04 +0900 70) });\\\\n9c6c41e4 src/features\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m/desktop-node/RipgrepClient.ts                             (Daichi Kimura 2026-07-14 00:32:04 +0900 71) \\\\n9c6c41e4 src/features/desktop-node/RipgrepClient.ts                             (Daichi Kimura 2026-07-14 00:3\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m2:04 +0900 72) function runProcess(\\\\n9c6c41e4 src/features/desktop-node/RipgrepClient.ts                             (Daichi Kimura 2026-07-14 00:32:04 +0900 73)   command: string,\\\\n9c6c41e4 src/features/desktop-nod\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0me/RipgrepClient.ts                             (Daichi Kimura 2026-07-14 00:32:04 +0900 74)   args: readonly string[],\\\\n9c6c41e4 src/features/desktop-node/RipgrepClient.ts                             (Daichi Kimura 2\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[7m\u001b[0m026-07-14 00:32:04 +0900 75)   cwd: string,\\\\n9c6c41e4 src/features/desktop-node/RipgrepClient.ts 