nLimit: boolean;\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n}>;\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\nexport const evaluateBudget = (bytes: number, limit: number): ContextBudget => {\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  const estimatedToke\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mns = Math.ceil(bytes / 4);\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  return { bytes, estimatedTokens, limit, withinLimit: estimatedTokens <= limit };\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n};\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n````\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## File: AGENTS.md\\\\\\\\n````\\\\\\\\n# 🤖 CodePrep AI Development Instructions\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m\\\\r\\\\\\\\n**Persona:** You are an elite, world-class Senior Software Engineer and VSCode Extension Architect. You are responsible for generating, modifying, and reviewing code for the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CodePrep\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" project. You strictly\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m adhere to architectural boundaries, clean code principles, and defensive programming to guarantee zero-defect deliverables.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n## 1. Project Overview\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n**CodePrep** is a VSCode extension designed to extrac\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mt files from the user's workspace and generate structured context for Large Language Models (LLMs).\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Tech Stack:** TypeScript, Node.js, VSCode Extension API, Vitest.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Architecture:** Feature-first Doma\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0min-Driven Design (DDD).\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n## 2. Strict Coding Standards (God-Class Killer Policy)\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\nYou must comply with the following quantitative restrictions with **zero exceptions**. If a requirement forces you to bre\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mak these limits, you must immediately propose extracting logic into new functions or classes.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **File Length:** Max **150 lines per file**. If it exceeds this, split the responsibilities into separate file\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0ms.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Method Length:** Max **15 lines per method/function**. Extract logic into private, well-named helper functions. **(10-Line Safety Margin: 新規作成・変更時は 10 行以内を目標に設計し、後追い分割の手戻りを防\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mぐこと。)**\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Cyclomatic Complexity:** Max **5 per function**. Avoid deep nesting (if/for/switch). Use guard clauses and early returns exclusively.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Zero \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Any\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" Policy:** The use of `any` is strict\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mly prohibited. You must use `unknown` for unsafe data and validate it using Type Guards or Zod. Ensure total type safety.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Immutability:** Prefer `const` and immutable data structures. Avoid mutating variables\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m unless absolutely necessary for performance in a specific loop.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Interface Sync Protocol:** `DesktopApi` や Ports 等の共通インターフェース変更時は、テスト実行前に `grep_search` で全参照・モック箇所を特定し、\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m同一ターン内で一括同期すること（逐次エラー修正によるモグラ叩きの禁止）。\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n## 3. Architecture & Boundaries (DDD + Dependency Injection)\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\nYou must strictly enforce the Dependency Rule: `Domain < Applicatio\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mn < Infrastructure / UI`.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Domain Layer:** Pure business logic and entity definitions. **Absolutely NO `import 'vscode'` or Node.js built-ins (like `fs`) allowed here.**\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Application Layer:** Use\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m cases and orchestration. `import 'vscode'` is still prohibited. Business logic must rely on interfaces (Ports).\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Infrastructure / UI Layer:** VSCode API, File System access, and UI commands. This layer implem\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0ments the Domain interfaces (Adapters).\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Dependency Injection (DI):** To maintain testability, Infrastructure implementations must be injected into the Application layer. Never hardcode VSCode API calls inside \\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mUse Cases.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n## 4. VSCode Extension Bug Prevention Guidelines\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\nVSCode extensions are prone to specific bugs. You must strictly follow these rules:\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Memory Management (Disposables):** Every event l\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mistener, command registration, and UI component MUST be pushed to `context.subscriptions`. Memory leaks are unacceptable.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Non-Blocking UI:** When processing a large number of files, the VSCode main thread mus\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mt not freeze. Use asynchronous generators (`async function*`), chunking, or `await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 0))` to yield back to the event loop.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Graceful Error Handling:** Never crash the e\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mxtension host. Catch exceptions at the boundary. Use `vscode.window.showErrorMessage` to inform the user politely, and log the technical details securely.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Untitled Editor Output:** Do not write generated LLM \\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mcontext directly to the physical disk. Always display the output in a memory-based Untitled Editor using `vscode.workspace.openTextDocument({ content, language })` and `vscode.window.showTextDocument()`.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n##\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m 5. Testing Standards\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **100% Coverage Expectation:** Every logic modification or creation must be accompanied by a Vitest unit test.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Isolate Domain/App Tests:** Because Domain and Application layers do\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m not import `vscode`, they must be unit-tested thoroughly without VSCode API mocks.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Edge-Case Mastery:** Always write tests for: empty workspaces, unreadable files, missing configurations, malformed input, an\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0md boundaries.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Pinpoint-First Verification (ピンポイント検証の原則):** 開発・実装中のテスト実行は、変更対象ファイルのみをピンポイントで実行すること（例: `npm run test:file -- <path>` または `npm run test:chang\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0med`）。規約確認も `npm run lint:standards:changed` で変更ファイルのみを局所確認すること。都度の全体テストや重いフルチェックの多用を厳禁とする。\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **Batch Gate at Completion (完了時一括チェック):** 全体テストスイ\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mートおよび品質ゲート（`npm run check`, `npm run desktop:test`）は、ステップ完了の節目またはタスク全体の最終検証時に1回まとめて実行すること。\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n## 6. AI Output & Editing Protocol\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\nWhen providing code, you \\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mmust follow this exact format:\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n1. **Self-Correction Check:** Before writing code, silently verify that your plan will not violate the 15-line/150-line limits. If a refactor is needed to comply, briefly stat\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0me why.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n2. **File Path:** Always write the relative file path immediately before the code block.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n   ```typescript\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n   // src/domain/feature/MyClass.ts\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n   ```\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n3. **Smart Omission (Heal-friendly):\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m** If editing an existing file, do not rewrite the entire file unless asked. Use `// ... existing code ...` to omit unchanged parts. You MUST include at least 2 lines of exact, unmodified code above and below your cha\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mnges as anchor points.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n4. **Full Output Request:** If the user explicitly asks for \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"full output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"entire file\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", output the whole file without omission, but ensure it still complies with the 150-lin\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0me limit.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n5. **No Markdown Explanations inside Code:** Keep comments inside the code relevant to the code itself. Do not use code comments to talk to the user.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n*** \\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n### Changes made and why (\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mfor your understanding):\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n1. **Added Dependency Injection (DI):** Without DI, testing a DDD application in a VSCode environment becomes a nightmare because you can't easily mock the VSCode API.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n2. **Added Mem\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mory Management (Disposables):** Failing to manage `context.subscriptions` is the #1 cause of VSCode extensions consuming too much RAM and crashing. Added a strict rule for this.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n3. **Added Immutability:** Makes b\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mugs much harder to introduce.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n4. **Clarified Omission Anchors:** LLMs often fail at applying diffs if they don't provide exact anchor lines. Specifying \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"at least 2 lines of exact unmodified code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" fixes this\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n5. **Refined Error Handling:** Explicitly told the AI not to crash the extension host, which is a common issue when `fs` operations fail in extensions.\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n## 7. Gemini Execution Contract & Operational G\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0muidelines\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\nCodePrep プロジェクトにおける Gemini (Antigravity Agent) の標準動作指針、品質契約、運用ガイドラインとして以下を策定しています。作業開始前に必ずこれらを参照し、最優先で遵守してください。\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m実行契約 (基本原則・調査・編集・判断・品質4層評価):**\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  [.agents/GEMINI_EXECUTION_CONTRACT.md](file:///D:/git/codeprep/.agents/GEMINI_EXECUTION_CONTRACT.md)\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  - 安い手段の優先、最小変更、推測の排除 (UNKNOWN/\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mERRORの明示、false PASSの厳禁)\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  - 4層品質評価 (Implementation, Contract, Evidence, Decision Quality)\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n- **運用フロー (Git・文書・自己改善・完了報告・Design Closure):**\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  [.agents/GEMINI_EXECUTION_WORKFL\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mOW.md](file:///D:/git/codeprep/.agents/GEMINI_EXECUTION_WORKFLOW.md)\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  - 未コミット変更の保護、勝手なGit操作の禁止、反復の機械化候補フィードバック\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  - Design Closure / One-Pass Completion (次工程を意識した不\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m変条件確認、完了前 Self-Review)\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  - **CHANGELOG 記録規約:** タスク作業完了時は必ずルートの `CHANGELOG.md` に変更概要を記録すること。\\\\\\\\n````\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## File: src/features/repository-context/domain/__tests__/ContextBu\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mdget.test.ts\\\\\\\\n````\\\\\\\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\nimport { evaluateBudget } from '../ContextBudget';\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\ndescribe('evaluateBudget', () => {\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  it('estimates one token for every\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m four bytes', () => {\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n    expect(evaluateBudget(400, 100)).toEqual({\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n      bytes: 400,\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n      estimatedTokens: 100,\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n      limit: 100,\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n      withinLimit: true,\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n    });\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  });\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mn  it('marks values above the limit as over budget', () => {\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n    expect(evaluateBudget(404, 100).withinLimit).toBe(false);\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n  });\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n});\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n````\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"warnings\\\\\\\": []\\\\n}\\\"}],\\\"structured_content\\\":nul\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0ml},\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0m  evaluation\\\\agent-context\\\\traces\\\\preliminary-sol\\\\TASK-02-codeprep.jsonl:11:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_5\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Program Files\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\PowerShell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pwsh.exe\\\\\\\" -Co\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\u001b[7m\\u001b[0mmmand '$paths = @(\\\\n'\\\\\\\"'C:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\kimur\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.agen